      "content": "that's a strong start. i really like the part about how not voting is actually empowering the wrong people. \n\ncould you expand on that part though? specifically, address the people who say that if all the candidates are corrupt or incompetent, then \"voting is a wasted effort\" or that it's better to abstain as a form of protest. i want the speech to shut that down—make it clear that their \"protest\" is actually just Cowardice 101 and that they're actually hurting the very cause they claim to care about. make it feel like their refusal to vote is a betrayal of their neighbors.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
